dawn: pin the 2026-10-30 tree with the crash fixes

The feed's pin (2026-06-10) segfaults on openwrt-ppe-nss: all three APs
running it crash-loop with exit_code 139 (SIGSEGV) within minutes, dying
around the inter-AP TCP handshake churn (connect_cb / client_notify_state
in tcpsocket.c), with procd backing off after a dozen respawns. The same
binary loops on every unit, so it is not a peer-version issue.

The tree after the pin carries the relevant fixes:

- 0a4ce31a5 iwinfo: deal with iwinfo_backends returning NULL
- 168286e42 ubus: reject beacon reports missing rcpi, rsni, or channel
- 167d424bb fix: only return true when hostapd_dir is actually configured
- 0d1ed7fa9 config: default duration to 150, not 0
  (the old default ships duration '0', which fails beacon requests)

PKG_MIRROR_HASH:=skip: the pin is a moving branch tip and its tarball
must not share a download name with the feed's own.

